# Terraform AWS Infrastructure — Private VPC, Subnet, Security Group & EC2

## 1. Project Overview

This project uses Terraform to provision and manage a private AWS-style infrastructure environment through the configured AWS-compatible endpoint at `http://aws:4566`.

The infrastructure consists of:
- A Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)
- A private subnet
- A security group
- An Amazon EC2 instance without a public IP address
- Terraform variables and outputs for configuration and verification

## 2. Objectives

- Create a VPC with a configurable CIDR block.
- Create a private subnet inside the VPC.
- Configure a security group that permits inbound traffic from the VPC CIDR.
- Deploy an EC2 instance in the private subnet.
- Prevent automatic assignment of a public IP address.
- Validate the Terraform configuration and verify the infrastructure plan.

